// English dialogue for Better Immersion for Athkatla: Temple District.
// Extracted from QCTEMP.d in CotSC translation Batch 13.
// Do not renumber these keys after community translations begin.

@1 = ~If I would take leadership over this city, I'd demolish all these temples on behalf of Gorellik.~
@2 = ~No! I don't take that into consideration. Our original creator and protector is Master of Hyenas! He took us under his wing, when none other deity would.~
@3 = ~Lass! Don't. The sources of education you are taking your guesses from are incorrect.~
@4 = ~I am not here to lecture an elf on theology! This rotting city needs a temple of Gorellik, and I will see it built, no matter what!~
@5 = ~This outfit looks stupid on you. Where'd you get it from, your mommies cabinet?~
@6 = ~You... mean... (She covers her face in her hands and runs off crying.)~
@7 = ~I can't be seen talking to you. Petty over there will be really unforgiving if I choose someone else to talk to. She's very mean and... insecure. Don't let her know I said that. She'll make a coat out of my skin.~
@8 = ~Wow. That was... amazing. She was always so insecure and jealous over everything. She treated me like a slave more than a friend. It's about time someone put her in her place. You have my thanks stranger.~
@9 = ~Really? I... I don't know how to thank you. I will kindly accept... thank you so much. I really appreciate it.~
@10 = ~Bah. You ain't know nothing of my pain. And life will not get better. I know exactly how unfair life is.~
@11 = ~Crusade of Caelar made me lose everything. Everything I had! I came to this city to seek shelter and instead I am still homeless. And hopeless.~
@12 = ~I am so sorry for your loss. I know what it's like to lose a home.~
@13 = ~Despair not. Just north of here lies temple of Helm. They shall welcome you with open arms.~
@14 = ~I am truly devastated to hear about your loss. This Caelar woman... news of her crusade reached my ears. People lost so much. I wish we could do something more about it.~
@15 = ~Caelar Argent caused many troubles. I assure you, we know what it's like. We've seen it first-hand up north.~
@16 = ~Would you accept this 100 gold coins from me. Just so you can get up on your feet a little.~
@17 = ~I am sorry to hear that. I hope life goes easier on you with time.~
@18 = ~How much more do I have to pray? I did nothing wrong. Littering is no crime. It's deviant but not criminal. I have no patience for this.~
@19 = ~What did you do?~
@20 = ~I littered. I threw some trash into the river and one of these punk clerics caught me and dragged me here. They said that if I can't behave I shall spent some time 'learning' how to behave. I am not allowed to leave until I regret the 'wrongfulness' of my ways. Tyrants!~
@21 = ~Stuff it in your... eh, nevermind. They'll let me out sooner or later.~
@22 = ~Gorellik? But... isn't he replaced by Yeenoghu?~
@23 = ~But... Gorellik didn't create your kind. He just...~
@24 = ~But...~
@25 = ~S-sure... yeah, absolutely. You're right. Can we... please, leave him?~
@26 = ~Listen here, lass! I care nay a whit for being crude, but last I checked, ye're no prize to look upon yerself! Ye've a bird's nest for hair, the temperament of a sweaty hobgoblin, and skin as slick and greasy as a blasted tasloi! Ye'd never give a proper dwarf the right urge to look twice at yer gangly form, much less find ye fetchin'! Bah!~
@27 = ~You should have behave like a person. Vandalism in a temple district goes against our principles.~
